## Final Judgement
Based on the fact-check record, the key finding is that while a civil lawsuit making allegations of a 1994 rape was filed against Donald Trump in 2016, multiple sources—including Snopes and CafeMom—state that the lawsuit was voluntarily dismissed in 2016 and was not active in 2020. The claim states Trump is "facing a court case" as of October 12, 2020, implying an active or pending case at that time. The evidence from reliable fact-checking sources and court reporting consistently indicates the case had been dismissed years prior and was not active in 2020.

The evidence is clear and consistent on the point that the lawsuit was not active in October 2020, so no further investigation is required. There is no lack of information to finalize the decision.

The claim that Donald Trump was facing an active court case for raping a teen in 1994 as of October 12, 2020, is explicitly refuted by the documented dismissal of the lawsuit prior to that date. Therefore, the conclusion is `refuted`.

